Package: resolve
Title: Predicting Sample Outcomes from Compositional Data
Version: 0.7.2
Authors@R:
    person("Gilles", "Colling", email = "gilles.colling@uliege.be", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Predict sample-level outcomes from compositional data (species lists,
    item sets, or any variable-length categorical inputs) using learned
    representations. Supports hash, embedding, rank-pool, and transformer
    encoding modes with a C++ core engine and optional GPU acceleration.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/gcol33/resolve
BugReports: https://github.com/gcol33/resolve/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
LinkingTo:
    Rcpp
Imports:
    Rcpp (>= 1.0.0),
    jsonlite,
    methods
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr,
    rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: The resolve_c shared library (a C ABI over the RESOLVE
    engine, bundling libtorch >= 2.0), loaded at run time. It is NOT needed to
    install or check this package. Install it afterwards with
    resolve.install_backend(), which downloads a prebuilt build into the user
    data directory, or point the RESOLVE_C_HOME environment variable at a
    directory that contains it. The dataset, training and prediction verbs
    require it; resolve.available() reports whether it is loaded.
LazyData: false
